        "denialFound": "None found, and none was asked for. The claim is a neutral benchmark that alleges nothing, so no party has anything to respond to.",
        "innocentReading": "India spends close to the peer-group norm. The 2.3% includes paramilitary spending, so it overstates the MoD-only burden, which PRS puts at about 1.9% for 2025-26. The Standing Committee's 3% figure is a domestic target, not a peer norm. These benign readings are already the claim's own reading. Nothing in it implies under- or over-spending or wrongdoing.",
