        "denialFound": "No institutional denial from the MHA or any state police was found, and none was sought by this record. At the launch, former DGP Prakash Singh disputed the definition of torture (\"What is torture? In India there is no definition of torture. Does a slap constitute torture? I don't think so\") and stressed that most respondents back legal procedure and human-rights training (https://www.livelaw.in/articles/launch-status-policing-report-india-report-2025-police-torture-288708). LeDroit India published a critique of bias and flaws in the method (https://ledroitindia.in/status-of-policing-in-india-report-2025-bias-flaws/). The report itself flags social-desirability bias (SPIR 2025, p.24, fn 1).",
