        "innocentReading": "Dassault had an MoU with Reliance going back to 2012 (the SC notes Reliance–Dassault contacts 'starting from the year 2012'). The offset guidelines leave the choice of Indian offset partner to the OEM. The 36-aircraft fly-away IGA dropped the 108 aircraft to be licence-built at HAL, so HAL's role ended for structural reasons. The price difference follows from changes in scope (India Specific Enhancements, weapons package, escalation and exchange-rate movement over 2007–2016). On a like-for-like basis, CAG found the 2016 contract 2.86% below the aligned 2007 bid. Hollande's quote may reflect what the French side understood about Indian preferences, not a direction from MoD, and he later said he did not know whether pressure had been applied.",
