        "innocentReading": "BEML had bought Tatra vehicles and kits for the Army under a long-running arrangement since 1986. It treated Tatra Sipox UK as the OEM's authorised marketing arm, so in its view this was not a prohibited middleman. On this reading the price gap reflects BEML's value-add, margins and kit assembly rather than a kickback. The CBI's own 2014 finding of insufficient evidence for a chargesheet is consistent with this reading. Against it, the reported documents show Tatra Sipox UK (incorporated 1994) predating Tatra Sipox a.s. (1998). That cuts against the \"subsidiary\" defence. It is why the matter remains an allegation and has not been dismissed.",
