        "innocentReading": "This was a summit-originated government-to-government deal. The PMO, and the French President's office on the other side, followed up on unresolved issues: sovereign guarantee, bank guarantee and general terms. Desk officials saw this as cutting across their formal negotiating channel and protested. The minister ruled that it was monitoring, not negotiation, and told the Defence Secretary to settle it with the Principal Secretary to the PM. The formal team (INT) kept negotiating, and the deal went through the DAC and CCS. This reading fits every document in hand as well as \"parallel negotiations over MoD's objection\" does.",
