        "denialFound": "This is a narrative with no accused party, so there is no denial as such. The government's position is on record: PIB says defence production hit an all-time high of about Rs 1.51 lakh crore in FY2024-25 (https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2154551) and exports reached Rs 23,622 crore in FY2024-25, up from under Rs 1,000 crore in 2014 (https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=2117348). These figures are self-reported and use a different metric from SIPRI TIV. The record does not cite them, and the strongestCounter would be stronger if it did.",
        "innocentReading": "India is a large military facing two hostile neighbours. It buys whole platforms, mainly combat aircraft and submarines, that it cannot yet build, and today's deliveries pay for contracts signed years ago. So a high import rank is compatible with real indigenisation progress: SIPRI itself credits domestic production for part of the decline. It is equally compatible with indigenisation stalling, since SIPRI 2026 also points to big new foreign orders and domestic delays. Rank alone settles neither case.",
        "reason": "The narrative record holds as a catalogue of a contested claim. Its strongestCase already says India ranks second, not first, and the cited SIPRI PDF confirms 8.3%, the 9.3% fall, Russia going from 72% to 36%, and SIPRI's link to domestic production. Calling it \"contested\" and laying out both cases is fair. It needs three fixes. First, one strongestCase statement is attributed to a source that does not contain it. Second, the test it set for itself (SIPRI 2021–25) has now been published and is not reflected. Third, \"contested\" understates the problem with the claim: the \"largest\" premise is false for both recent windows, and the inference to \"failed\" does not follow from the data. The same lens applied to UPA-II gives the same verdict, so it cannot single out Make in India. Treat the assessment as analytic (our own inference); SIPRI figures quoted alone can be cited as documented.",
