        "denialFound": "Yes, a denial exists. BEML CMD V.R.S. Natarajan said in 2012 that the Army chief's assessment was wrong, demanded an apology, threatened a defamation suit, and said the trucks had 60% indigenous content even without transfer of technology (reported in the Ajai Shukla Broadsword post of March 2012 and in Deccan Herald coverage). The CBI's own August 2014 closure report (\"insufficient evidence to file chargesheet\", Firstpost, cited at https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ravi_Rishi) is the institutional counter. Against that: MoD suspended Natarajan in June 2012 and suspended dealings with Vectra (Deccan Herald). None of this is in the record.",
        "innocentReading": "BEML held a licence and joint-venture arrangement with Tatra and Vectra. Routing purchases through the Hong Kong and UK group entities can be explained by group tax structuring and by the DPSU's integration and indigenisation markup, not only by a protected middleman. After two years the CBI found the evidence insufficient for a chargesheet. The Rs 14 crore offer, alleged by the Army chief, shows that he refused it. It does not show that earlier tranches were corrupt, a point the record's own strongestCounter makes correctly.",
        "reason": "The one source cited, a Wikipedia stub, supports \"about 7,000 trucks over more than two decades\" and an alleged overpricing chain through Vectra-group entities. It does not support \"a middleman protected by BEML\". That phrase names a DPSU as protecting a beneficiary without a primary record, which the force contract forbids. The narrative's strongestCounter and whatWouldChangeThis rest on \"no CBI outcome opened\", but the outcome is easy to find. The CBI filed a closure report in August 2014, the special court declined to accept it in November 2019, and the bribe-offer case is still on trial (charges framed in 2019, upheld by the HC in 2022). BEML's denial is also on record. Keeping \"speculative\" because only a stub was read is a retrieval failure, not a finding. Reworded, the claim can stand as an allegation: allegations by the Army chief and by the CBI at FIR stage, with the closure report and BEML's denial as the counter.",
