        "recommendedTier": "alleged",
        "sourceCheck": "partially",
        "denialFound": "No Congress response to the 2026-08-06 dismissal was found. I searched for one (The Federal, DNA and TOI reports carry no party statement). Not asked. Congress's long-standing position is the Delhi HC 2004 acquittal (\"public servants completely absolved\", para 140, https://indiankanoon.org/doc/561739/). Sten Lindström said in 2012 that Rajiv Gandhi did nothing wrong (BBC 2012-04-25, cited on https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bofors_scandal). The other side is on record too. Arun Jaitley (BJP) listed the CBI's lapses. CMM Vinod Yadav, on the withdrawal of the case against Quattrocchi, said: \"I agree that there are certain malafide intentions in the case and there is no doubt in that\" (Wikipedia, \"Allegations against CBI\").",
        "innocentReading": "There is a duller explanation that fits the same facts. The evidence was foreign-sourced commercial documents that were hard to prove under Sections 63 and 78(6) of the Evidence Act, which is what Kapoor J held. The key accused died: Rajiv Gandhi in 1991, Bhatnagar and Chadha in 2001, Quattrocchi in 2013. Extradition from Malaysia and Argentina failed on legal grounds. Delay piled up under every government, including the CBI's 4,522-day-late SLP under NDA. On this reading the case ended because the evidence was weak and time ran out, which is The Federal's account, not because anyone was shielded. The UPA-era unfreezing and withdrawal can also be read as the CBI accepting, after 2004, that it could not prove its case.",
        "reason": "The narrative passes only as \"contested\". Its own framing claims no more than that, and the record really does split. The agent-side payments are documented. Specific Congress-era acts that benefited the agent Quattrocchi are on record, and a magistrate called the case's handling malafide. Against that, a High Court, after 13 years of CBI investigation, found no evidence that any public servant received money, and governments of both kinds held the file without getting a conviction. The source chain is weaker than the record claims. strongestCase's facts about the 1993 departure and the two failed extraditions are not in either cited source; Wikipedia mentions only Argentina. They are confirmed by The Federal, which is not cited. strongestCounter misattributes the \"entitled to be seen as innocent\" sentence to the court's own holding. And the actual strongest case (the London account unfreezing, the red corner notice withdrawal, CMM Yadav's malafide remark) is left out, while a single-sourced claim of \"government pressure\" on The Hindu is put in. As an assertion, \"Congress protected recipients\" is a named party's allegation (BJP/Jaitley) with a judicial contra, so it belongs in the alleged tier, not higher.",
