        "innocentReading": "Commission payments to agents and consultants on a 556 million euro contract were described as bribes by Italian prosecutors. On the full evidence, the Italian courts found it insufficient to prove corruption: Busto Arsizio in 2014 acquitted Orsi and Tyagi of corruption; the Milan retrial acquitted in 2018; Cassation made that final in 2019; and Brescia acquitted Haschke on 30 Jun 2025. The 2014 corporate settlement (patteggiamento) is not an admission of guilt under Italian law and may have been a commercial decision to close the case. India's cancellation rested on breach of the integrity pact (undisclosed agents), which is a lower bar than proof of bribery. The Indian case is still before charge framing after 12 years, so in India nothing has been tested.",
