        "denialFound": "The government's response is already in the cited PRS source, and the record leaves it out. PRS p.2: \"According to the Ministry of Defence, spending 3% of India's GDP on the defence sector will lead to much higher allocations which the defence services may not be able to absorb.\" PRS adds that 3% in 2025-26 would mean Rs 10.7 lakh crore, or 21% of central spending. PRS also notes that \"in 2023-24 and 2024-25, the allocation for the capital budget of the armed forces has been in line with their projections.\" Source: https://prsindia.org/files/budget/budget_parliament/2025/DFG_Analysis_2025-26_Defence.pdf. The Ministry contradicts itself: in its 15th FC memo it said the shortfalls caused \"serious capability gaps\". Both statements are on the record.",
