        "reason": "The narrative stands as \"contested\". Every number checks against the opened PDFs: SC 2018 \"about 3% of GDP\"; \"1.9% of its GDP\" for 2025-26; 17% in 2014-15 to 13% in 2025-26; capital outlay \"less than 30%\" (28% in 2025-26); Rs 9.01 vs 17.46 lakh crore; SIPRI 5th, $86.1bn, 2.3%, global 2.5%. It is a value question, and the record does not dress it up as fact. But the strongestCounter contains a false statement and leaves out the strongest counter in its own source. \"The 3% target has no peer basis\" is wrong. In SIPRI Table 1, the US (3.4), Poland (4.2) and four others are above 3%, and NATO's Hague Summit Declaration of 25 June 2025 commits allies to 3.5% of GDP on core defence by 2035 (https://www.nato.int/en/about-us/official-texts-and-resources/official-texts/2025/06/25/the-hague-summit-declaration). Meanwhile the MoD's own \"may not be able to absorb\" statement, the actual government response, is left out. These are field errors to fix, not a refutation of the claim. The tier is analytic: the numbers it rests on are documented, but the calibration is our own inference.",
