        "denialFound": "The accused officers' answer is the judicial record. Rath was acquitted of all charges by the AFT on 5 Sep 2014, with Rs 1 lakh costs and benefits restored at 12% interest (https://www.deccanchronicle.com/140906/nation-current-affairs/article/lt-general-p-k-rathretd-cleared-sukna-scam). The tribunal found the trial 'influenced and vitiated' and blamed then-Army chief V K Singh (https://www.ibtimes.co.in/sukna-land-deal-lt-gen-rath-acquitted-claims-vk-singh-filed-case-revenge-608445). The SC set aside Prakash's GCM on 24 Jan 2019 (https://indiankanoon.org/doc/156623410/). The other side also answered: V K Singh 'hits back' and urged MoD to appeal the AFT order (Deccan Herald, https://www.deccanherald.com/india/v-k-singh-hits-back-2205886). I found no record of an SC appeal by the Union against Rath's acquittal. I searched and that absence is unconfirmed, not proven.",
